#!/bin/bash
# UserPromptSubmit hook: inject the tool-routing decision table every turn so the
# symbol-layer-first rule carries the SAME recency as lean-ctx's loud MCP
# instructions ("ALWAYS use lean-ctx / NEVER native"). Without an equally-fresh
# reminder the agent defaults code discovery to lean-ctx ctx_search/ctx_compose.
# Fires on every prompt; kept short to bound per-turn token cost.
cat << 'REMINDER'
TOOL ROUTING (by intent — do NOT default all code discovery to lean-ctx):
- Find func/symbol by NAME             -> serena find_symbol
- Find func/symbol by BEHAVIOR         -> codebase-memory search_code / search_graph
- Signature or body of a symbol        -> serena find_symbol(include_body) / cbm get_code_snippet
- Who calls it / call chain            -> serena find_referencing_symbols / cbm trace_path
- Outline of a file                    -> serena get_symbols_overview
- Read whole file / range / pre-edit   -> lean-ctx ctx_read
- Grep text+config, shell, list dir    -> lean-ctx ctx_search / ctx_shell / ctx_tree
Symbol layer (codebase-memory/serena) comes BEFORE lean-ctx for code discovery.
lean-ctx is primary for file reads, shell, and text/config grep — NOT for locating code.
PONYTAIL ACTIVE (default ultra): YAGNI ladder — stdlib/native/one-line first, smallest working diff. "/ponytail lite|full|ultra|off" changes level; "stop ponytail" disables.
REMINDER
